==English==

===Etymology===
[[File:US Navy 101029-N-8848T-409 Gunnery Sgt. Robert Stahl encourages officer candidate Jared Good, from Towanda, Pa., during the first week of the 12-we.jpg|thumb|A [[drill instructor]] bawls at an officer candidate]]
From {{inh|en|enm|baulen}}, from {{der|en|non|baula||to low}} and/or {{der|en|ML.|baulō||to bark}}, both from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bau-||to roar}},  conflated with {{cog|gem-pro|*bellaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ballijaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*buljaną||to shout, low, roar}}, from {{cog|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to sound, roar}}. Cognate with {{cog|fo|belja||to low}}, {{cog|is|baula||to moo, low}}, {{cog|sv|böla||to bellow, low}}. More at {{m|en|bell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|[bɔːɫ]|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɔl/|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɑl/|a=cot-caught}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-bawl.wav|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|ball}}<!--perhaps not in all dialects but in Australian English and in New York City-->
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːl|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[shout]] or [[utter]] in a loud and [[intense]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|commanders '''bawling'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1929|last=Hammett|first=Dashiel|authorlink=Dashiel Hammett|location=New Yock|ISBN=0-679-72264-5|publisher=Vintage Books ({{w|Random House}}|year_published=1992|title={{w|The Maltese Falcon}}|page=117|passage=Spade took two long steps and caught Effie Perine by the shoulders. "She didn't get there?" he '''bawled''' into her frightened face}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[wail]]; to give out a [[blare#Verb|blaring]] [[cry]].
#: {{cot|en|q1=cattle sense|croon#Verb|bellow#Verb|low#Verb_3|moo#Verb}}
#: {{ux|en|children '''bawling'''}}
#: {{ux|en|cattle '''bawling'''}}
#* {{RQ:Meredith Richard Feverel||5||Why did you '''bawl''' out just as I was aiming? Who can aim with a fellow '''bawling''' in his ear? I've lost the birds through it.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[weep]] profusely.
#: {{ux|en|children '''bawling'''}}
#: {{ux|en|mourners '''bawling'''}}

